# R12: Gail Patrini, the housekeeper sewn inside the stuffed bear (H15, the trophy room). Speaker gail_patrini; memento memento_silver_pin / memento_pin.
# Gail speaks NO words (roaring, then wordless and bewildered): the Narrator carries the whole scene, so no gail_patrini line exists. The voice lane has no job here.
# FINAL-WORDED: every Narrator line below is voiced; no line changes once the voice lane starts (new lines are fine).
# Wiring assumptions: the prop h15_bear (found by the trophy room's skill challenge, or given away by the roar after round 6) calls gail:start; freeing her is
# cutting the stitches (the book's Utilize action), with no roll; cutscenes ch_gail_freed (the bear with her face at its chest) and ch_gail_freed_2 (the
# sawdust, the pin, the fade) read the lines under them.
# Drafted by Gemini (gemini_r12_gail/brief.md, reply_raw.json), edited; see that folder's README.md.

~ start
if flag.memento_pin
-> done
endif
Narrator: That roar presses hard behind your eyes, and all along the walls the stuffed heads set to rattlin' in their sockets.
Narrator: Right in the middle stands a great dusty bear on a timber block, with a woman's pale face sewn into the fur of its chest, mouth wide open.
Narrator: Thick wax cord holds the hide together down the seam, pulled coarse and tight by a heavy hand.
interject class:cleric: Someone bound her spirit into this poor beast, and we cannot leave her to suffer it.
interject class:rogue: Hold the light steady a second, that heavy thread will give if I get a blade under the knot.
-> menu

~ menu
* [Insight DC 12] Look past the roar into her eyes. -> look_ok | look_miss
* Cut the stitches open. -> free
* Step back from the bear. -> END

~ look_ok
Narrator: You look past the noise into the wet dark of her eyes, and there ain't a speck of anger in them, only a terrible begging.
Narrator: She is hollerin' the way an iron bell rings when a cruel hand will not let go of the rope.
-> menu

~ look_miss
Narrator: The din hammers too loud against your skull to read her face, leaving only a wide mouth and a wall of sound.
-> menu

~ free
cutscene ch_gail_freed
Narrator: The heavy threads part one after another like old canvas tearing, and that awful roar cracks in half and breaks off.
Narrator: In the quiet that follows, the woman's eyelids flutter slow, like folks wakin' up in a strange bed after a fever.
cutscene ch_gail_freed_2
Narrator: She stares down at her own pale hands as though she has never seen them before.
Narrator: Her fingers close on a small silver pin at her collar, and she drives it deep into the bear's leather snout while dry sawdust sifts around her knees.
Narrator: She looks up at you, bewildered and unafraid, before she thins away like warm breath off a cold windowpane.
cutscene end
give memento_silver_pin
set memento_pin
Narrator: That silver pin stands bright in the dark leather of the snout, and when you draw it free, it slides out easy, like it was waitin' to be asked.
approve tobin_hayward +1 rook_coldwake +1 lucan_houndstooth +1: You cut a trapped woman out of the bear that held her
-> END

~ done
Narrator: The bear is only an old moths' nest now, dull glass and dry stuffing in the cold draft, and the room rests quiet at last.
-> END
